<title>USA: Navistar says agreement reached with CAW.</title>
<headline>Navistar says agreement reached with CAW.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Navistar International Corp said Monday it reached a tentative agreement on a new labor pact with the Canadian Auto Workers union.</p>
<p>Details of the agreement with union employees at the company's assembly plant in Chatham, Ontario, were not disclosed.</p>
<p>A ratification vote on the tentative agreement is scheduled in Chatham on October 27, 1996, by CAW Local 127. The Chatham plant employs about 1,600 workers, with 1,300 of them represented by the local.</p>
<p>Navistar manufacturers buses and heavy duty trucks. Its stock closed down 1/4 at 9-1/4 Monday.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
